Brief c2326ca6; on-spec/native ruling d668cde0; CPU-cached R8 shape approved 785dc42e, including the four default-only Glyph callers. Shared-file coordination: Seraph ae290a9f and Nyx 39be6791/d6c9054b confirm no overlapping renderer/atoms/components edits; TaskRow is untouched.
One general Prim::TextShadow, optional retained Glyph/Text property. Actual glyph/ink-overlap coverage is zero-padded and separably Gaussian blurred on a cache miss (sigma = blur radius / 2 in device pixels), then stored under glyph/phase/scale/sigma in the existing bounded R8 atlas/LRU. Color and integer translation add no cache key. Existing foreground and WGSL/material paths are unchanged; one extra flat quad per visible shadowed coverage component, no extra pass.
SeatRow waiting glyph requests amber, 6px blur, [0,0] offset as lab.css:257; kind text inherits it. Other Glyph callers default None. Grade and ancestor-opacity fields are checked; Text shadow color is independent of foreground alpha. Shadow is ink overflow and does not affect layout.
Sources: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-decor-3/#text-shadow-property ; https://drafts.csswg.org/css-backgrounds-3/#shadow-blur . CSS permits per-glyph shadowing; no whole-string bitmap cache was introduced.
GPU regression uses an independent 2-D convolution of a GPU-readback glyph mask on light/dark backgrounds, blur 0/6, integer offsets, quarter-pixel source phase, translucent foreground/shadow, transparent skip and repeated-frame identity/cache reuse. Dedicated new probe is at DPR1; no new full DPR2/fractional-DPR shadow matrix is claimed.
Real GPU probe at 12px “?”: one blur, 780 shadow-mask bytes / 876 total coverage bytes, 2 total misses; changed color/integer offset and repeats leave misses/blurs/bytes unchanged, with exactly one additional emitted shadow quad per render. Transparent shadow adds zero quads/blur. Full counters below.
